  "discussion": {
    "headline": "warmth, humidity and storms to return late this week",
    "dateLine": "11:00 a.m. Tuesday, August 25, 2026",
    "excerpt": "The last week of August kicked off on a partly-to-mostly sunny, cooler and less humid note. In the wake of Sunday's cold frontal passage, northwesterly winds of 8-16 mph ushered a refreshing and even fall-like air mass into the Commonwealth. High temperatures were around 5°F below average Monday afternoon, and dewpoints bottomed out in the low-to-mid 50s. …",
